# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
# plan.txt — copy to the repo root and fill in. Delete what you don't need.
# Prose works; the KEY: lines are what make execution precise.
# Full spec: skills/java-expert/references/plan-txt-spec.md
# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------

GOAL: <one sentence: the outcome, not the activity>

STACK: java=<17|21|25|27> build=<maven|gradle> framework=<spring-boot@4.1|jakarta-ee@11|quarkus|none> packaging=<jar|war> db=<postgresql|mysql|none>

# Hard limits. Recognized: no-new-deps, java=17-only, keep-public-api,
# keep-behavior, offline, no-schema-change, war=<container>, minimal-diff
CONSTRAINT: <constraint>
CONSTRAINT: <constraint>

# Known landmines. These prevent an agent from "helpfully" breaking things.
RISK: <e.g. deployed on Tomcat 9 today — do not introduce jakarta.* imports>
RISK:

# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
# Tasks — execute in order. One unit of work each.
# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------

TASK: <imperative: what must exist when this is done>
  FILES: <comma-separated paths, best guess>
  AC: <observable, testable acceptance criterion>
  AC: <second criterion, if needed>
  TEST: <the command or test that proves it>

TASK: <next task>
  AC:
  TEST:

TASK: <next task>
  AC:
  TEST:

# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
# Global definition of done. Anything written after this line is OUT OF SCOPE.
# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
DONE: clean build passes; new behavior has a failing-first test; no new
P0/P1 findings; artifact inspected if packaging=war; README updated.

# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
# Optional / future — explicitly not part of this run
# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
# - <nice to have>
